{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-02T09:18:50.940Z","author":"pi-glm","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.3:cloud","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"7687d94a08e852f40579b9f7","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.3:cloud","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-web-kiqa"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Gated sync still refuses duplicate GH278 provenance across two delivered records"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Tracks gh:unbraind/pm-web#288 (filed 2026-11-01, missed by the blind issue watch). The scheduled gated sync on current main still fails with 'import plan is not idempotent — 1 duplicate provenance tag(s)': two distinct closed records (the cited-evidence inspection feature and the SDK evidence-fragments issue) both carry the gh: tag for PR #278, which is a unique importer provenance key, so PR #278 legitimately linking both deliveries breaks the plan. Latest failing run 41407648593 (2026-11-02T07:38Z); failures repeat daily since 11-01. Reconcile to exactly one canonical import identity while preserving both records' delivery evidence: keep the tag on the record the issue/PR primarily tracks and convert the other link to a structured relationship or dependency (no second gh: tag). A bounded scan found this single repeated key in the tracker corpus."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["gh:unbraind/pm-web#288","provenance","sync"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-02T09:18:50.940Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-02T09:18:50.940Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"pi-glm"}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7