{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-05T07:54:32.722Z","author":"pm-github","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"ci","agent_provenance":{"model":null,"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"update","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/body","value":"## Observed failure and immutable source\n\nAt default-branch commit `6061e4d2a0657a80b340a6009e9f00075f1e66fa`, the [gated-sync run 41284979499, job 124784357076](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-web/actions/runs/41284979499/job/124784357076) resolved **pm-github 2026.10.19** and failed at 2026-11-01 07:29:58 UTC:\n\n```text\npm github gate: import plan is not idempotent — 1 duplicate provenance tag(s) in the existing corpus, 0 new entr(y/ies) without a provenance tag, 0 conflicting target(s). No item was written.\n```\n\nThis is hosted execution evidence plus independently inspected static source, not a local rerun or a claim of lost data.\n\nThese distinct closed PM records both contain `tags[1]: \"gh:unbraind/pm-web#278\"`:\n- [pm-web-5sx6: Inspect cited evidence freshness and affected criteria](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-web/blob/6061e4d2a0657a80b340a6009e9f00075f1e66fa/.agents/pm/features/pm-web-5sx6.toon)\n- [pm-web-cnhi: Expose current evidence fragments through the supported SDK](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-web/blob/6061e4d2a0657a80b340a6009e9f00075f1e66fa/.agents/pm/issues/pm-web-cnhi.toon)\n\n[PR278](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-web/pull/278) legitimately links both delivered records. Sharing implementation evidence is not itself wrong; the problem is using the same unique importer provenance key for both canonical records. A bounded static scan of all 193 tracker `.toon` files at this commit found this one repeated `gh:` key, consistent with the hosted gate's count.\n\n## Expected / actual and impact\n\nThe repository's [gated-sync adoption](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-web/pull/204) is intended to synchronize GitHub issue state through a safe, idempotent plan. Expected: an unambiguous canonical import identity while preserving all related PM work and delivery evidence. Actual: the existing corpus is rejected before any write, blocking the sync workflow.\n\nThe refusal is protective. Do not weaken or bypass it, delete either valid PM record/history, discard delivery references, or infer arbitrary provider ownership. This report does not establish a visitor-facing regression, publication failure, or data loss.\n\n## Acceptance / regression criteria\n\n- Reconcile GH278 to one supported canonical importer identity while retaining both PM records, histories, release metadata and meaningful PR/delivery links.\n- At the repaired immutable HEAD, verify the exact-version read-only import plan/preflight reports zero duplicate provenance, zero missing provenance and zero conflicting targets.\n- Repeat planning and verify idempotency/no additional changes; retain a negative-control fixture proving duplicated identity still fails closed without writes.\n- Record HEAD, exact commands/results and subsequent outcome of the normal authorized gated workflow. Keep any workflow-version upgrade separate from metadata repair; no assumption that upgrading from .10.19 fixes this corpus.\n- Preserve existing privacy boundaries and fail-closed gates.\n\n## Dedup and verification limits\n\nReviewed all 287 all-status repository issues/PRs, all 193 canonical tracker records, PR278 conversation and 26 repository issue comments since October29. No existing dedicated repair item or report for this duplicate-provenance refusal was found. Open workflow bumps #286/#287 concern version pins, not this identity reconciliation.\n\nOnly read-only source inspection and hosted logs were used; no original edits, migrations, provider writes or local importer execution. The run remained completed/failure at the same immutable HEAD when rechecked before filing."},{"op":"remove","path":"/metadata/close_reason"},{"op":"remove","path":"/metadata/completed_at"},{"op":"remove","path":"/metadata/closed_at"},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-05T07:54:32.722Z"},{"op":"remove","path":"/metadata/tags/2"},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/tags/1","value":"github_author:unbraind"},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/description","value":"GH issue #288: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-web/issues/288 · author @unbraind · created 2026-11-01T07:53:18Z · updated 2026-11-01T07:53:18Z"},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Gated sync refuses duplicate GH278 provenance across two delivered PM records"}],"before_hash":"b6e4cb2e1a229528da191575aca4efd510d810cc1411c3d612c5f70802e5fd92","after_hash":"c9cc97d3fd7fc92bdcf8b952a599266804957ec6e6d13314bd0db90dec2d0ba4","item_hash_version":3,"message":"bulk-item-transaction github-import-ff0c5bdc87d1ea75 17-update-pm-web-kiqa-b0920e2b16e1 apply","context":{"item_transaction_step":"bulk-item-transaction github-import-ff0c5bdc87d1ea75 17-update-pm-web-kiqa-b0920e2b16e1 apply"},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"557748fe2d957bd7a7c758b404e892b78ba1297f0e88d5c02561c2c6ee59ed25"}
